====Synonyms====
* {{l|is|hross}}, {{l|is|klár}}

====Usage notes====
The noun ''hestur'' is often used by native speakers to determine the case of a noun, as every singular indefinite form is different. This is done by substituting the word (whose case is unknown) with the appropriate form of ''hestur'', e.g.
: ''[[ég#Icelandic|ég]] [[borða]] [[brauð]].'' (I [[eat]] [[bread]])
becomes
: ''[[ég#Icelandic|ég]] [[borða]] '''hest'''. (I [[eat]] a [[horse]])
and because we know ''hest'' to be the accusative of hestur (and can't possibly be any other case), the word ''[[brauð]]'' must here also be in the accusative case.
To find the case forms of ''hestur'' (or any other noun) a certain set of prepositions is used (except for the nominative, where the noun is made the subject of a clause with reversed word order):
: [[hér]] [[vera#Icelandic|er]] '''hestur''' ({{nominative}}) = here is a '''horse'''
: [[um]] '''[[hest]]''' ({{accusative}}) = about a '''horse'''
: [[frá]] '''[[hesti]]''' ({{dat}}) = from a '''horse'''
: [[til]] '''[[hests]]''' ({{gen}}) = to a '''horse'''

